  "hints": [
    "Count ways to form each target prefix using source characters processed so far.",
    "There is one way to form the empty target. A matching source character adds the count for the preceding target prefix.",
    "For each source character, iterate target lengths downward and add ways[length-1] when the last target character matches.",
    "The downward update is essential: it prevents a single source character from filling multiple target positions."
  ],
  "editorial": "Maintain one count per target-prefix length, initially one for the empty prefix and zero otherwise. A source character may be skipped or used to extend a matching shorter prefix. Process target lengths from right to left so every extension uses counts from before the current source position. The result counts index selections, not distinct resulting strings. Python integers preserve intermediate counts exactly; only the final result has the source's 32-bit guarantee. The independent oracle enumerates fixed-size combinations of source indexes.",
